  "note": "loso-institution (23 institution folds, 1,120 dev subjects) CLOSING CONFIRMATION run of the UNCHANGED iter16 working tree (measurer makes ZERO code edits, no revert, no edit). Code = iter13 accepted tree (Gordon+HCP as ONE concatenated member, Power, Markov; each own training-fold-only log-Euclidean tangent space + age/sex; L2 logistic LOGREG_C=1e-2; ASD_WEIGHT_GRID 1.0/2.0/4.0; members combined ONLY via neuroasd.ensemble.stack_scores on grouped training-fold OOF columns with one logistic META_C=1e-2; training-fold-only UNMAPPED OOF cut at the 73% control-recall floor, per held-out subject, one fit per fold, no test-fold/best-epoch selection; per-subject Ledoit-Wolf shrunk FC; top-K |t| masks K=20000/8000/12000) PLUS the single landed change: a SECOND pre-registered independently regularized L2 logistic at SECOND_MEMBER_C=1e-1 fitted beside LOGREG_C=1e-2 on the SAME training rows, SAME training-only edge mask and SAME ASD class weight, Gordon+HCP member ONLY, decision values combined by a FIXED 50/50 mean (neuroasd.ensemble.average_scores), applied identically to inner-OOF columns and the final training refit; Power/Markov single-scale; meta-learner, ASD weight grid, stacked-OOF cut rule and 73% floor untouched. FRAMING: CLOSING CONFIRMATION ONLY - the screen AUC discriminator (0.8574 vs iter13 0.8564 = 0.03 fold SEM) and the loso-site discriminator (0.8076 vs 0.8064 = 0.055 fold SEM) were both MISSED, so the fixed dual-C average is already refuted as a ranking gain. Nothing here may be described as an improvement. PRE-DECLARED DISCRIMINATOR: institution AUC must exceed the iter13 institution reference 0.7901 by more than ~1 fold SEM (iter13 institution fold SD 0.0947, SEM ~0.024); flat or down => mechanism REFUTED on all three splits. ACCEPTANCE TEST vs iter13 institution (ASD 0.6610, control 0.7735, BA 0.7172, AUC 0.7901): institution ASD >= 0.6610 + 0.3pp = 0.6640, institution control >= 0.73 AND no more than 0.5pp below 0.7735 i.e. >= 0.7685; report whether all three arms pass simultaneously. Report fold-mean [fold SD] for ASD recall, control recall, BA, accuracy, AUC; gate margin; PASS/FAIL; exit code and runtime (screen 25.1 min, loso-site 62.5 min with two logits per weight point - flag if institution is far over its 120-min budget). Report count and names of folds below 0.73 control recall (floor_passed is mean-level only; 8/23 site folds were below it). SECONDARY READOUT: verbatim measurement_notes/protocol_notes and any end-of-fit_predict stderr line carrying neuroasd.model.LAST_FEATURE_COUNTERS; empty for twelve consecutive runs - if empty again, report plain empty and do not infer that the LW shrinkage, top-K mask, or second-logit paths fired. No gates change, no rescale/remap/recalibration of the cut, no promotion beyond this stage.",
